      "spam": false,
      "value": "(SOLUTION)\nI had this problem too at one point. Turns out that the text seemingly was not an error, but a general warning that shows up no matter what. Or at-least that's what I believe it is, being its never caused any problems and is always there.\n\nIn order to fix the incapability to select any options I had created a new Unity Project the same way when creating my first. Once the new Project was created I went into the old Project save file (~while the new project is loaded) location and double-clicked the asset package containing my Avatar. This imports the old asset data so that no progress was lost. Done. Nothing is lost, and all is good.\n\nI have no idea why this happens, but as far as I know this is just a mystery bug with no given Error for it. I do have an idea that may fix it, but i have not tried it. You might also be able to re-import the VRChat SDK package and it might replace the broke data.\n\nIf this worked for you i would suggest marking your title with \"(FIX)\" so others will know to see the solution.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
